# Cursor Rules — korays-framework (V2)

## Project
Topical Authority Operating System (V2).
TypeScript (Node.js) orchestrator with AI-agent architecture.
Entry-point: src/cli.ts. Core library: src/ package.

## Language & Environment
- TypeScript 5.x
- Node.js (ES Modules)
- Target: ES2022
- Module Resolution: NodeNext

## Code Style
- Strict typing on all variables, functions, and classes.
- Use Interfaces/Types from `src/types.ts`.
- Use `winston` for logging — never `console.log` in library code (CLI is OK).
- Use `zod` for all data validation and AI schema enforcement.

## Architecture Rules
- Provider-agnostic: All AI interactions must use `AIClient` interface.
- Agent-based: Logic is split into specialized agents (Clustering, Hierarchy, Brief).
- Orchestrator-led: `src/orchestrator.ts` manages the pipeline flow.
- Separation of Concerns: Data collection, NLP, Agents, and Exporters must remain decoupled.

## Pipeline Data Flow
Seeds → Query Data → SERP Snapshot → Clustering → Hierarchy → Entity Extraction → Brief Generation → Exporters

## Testing
- Framework: `vitest`
- Use fixtures for SERP and AI responses.
- No real network calls in unit tests.

## Key Files
1. src/types.ts         — data model
2. src/orchestrator.ts  — pipeline orchestration
3. src/core/aiClient.ts — AI abstraction
4. src/cli.ts           — CLI entry point
